# Races reported entirely inside uninstrumented third-party Vulkan components (the Mesa lavapipe
# driver threads and the Khronos validation layer). Reviewed individually: the Mingol frames in these
# reports are only callers (vkDestroySwapchainKHR / vkCreateDevice) made under our queue mutex after
# vkQueueWaitIdle. Suppressed by module so a race in Mingol code itself still fails the test.
race:libvulkan_lvp.so
race:libVkLayer_khronos_validation.so
# The system libLLVM that lavapipe JIT-compiles shaders with (uninstrumented; its internal locks are
# invisible to TSan, so allocator/StringMap accesses between llvmpipe worker threads look like races).
# Every report seen is entirely inside llvmpipe worker threads; no Mingol frame is involved.
race:libLLVM
# Lock-order cycle between the validation layer's own internal locks (seen once in ~25 runs, while we
# destroy the device). None of the mutexes in the cycle belong to Mingol.
deadlock:libVkLayer_khronos_validation.so
deadlock:libvulkan_lvp.so
